I'm assuming your predicament essentially boils down to one thing: the
only peaceful priest you've encountered has all the gold you've found.
I can think of two ways around this:

1) kill him and take all the gold.  There's one more guaranteed
peaceful priest a little later, but you have to storm the Castle first.

2) steal the gold, pacify him, then buy the protection back from the
same priest.  I successfully did this once by polymorphing into a
leprechaun, hitting him ONE time, polymorphing back, and using a magic
harp.  This strategy depends on having multiple magical items, though,
and is pretty dangerous.

As far as other ways of lowering AC: the classic way (besides finding
better armor, of course) is to read lots of blessed scrolls of enchant
armor.  If you're not finding these, you can make them with a magic
marker and water-blanked scrolls, or by polymorphing other scrolls.

Finally, praying a lot under the right circumstances can get you divine
protection.  This takes a long, long time though, and usually means
hanging around an altar and sacrificing for many thousands of turns.



